Rerun`), so `Build` stays pure and Resume replays the same plan. The engineer's first `done` in a round consumes it: its close-out clears `ard:triage:lead:done` (`Plan.Clear`, removed in the request phase before the requests are added, 404 counting as success) and adds `ard:pending`, so the lead runs first, and persists the other triage roles that had finished `done` (`Plan.Rerun`). The lead's close-out in that round re-requests those roles and clears their `:done` (roles no longer configured are skipped), so all finish before the gate. A human re-request of the engineer sees no open round and does not re-arm again. The engineer may declare `inputs:` (`path`, `provider` `human` or `worker`, optional https `url`), parsed from the redacted role file and stored in the plan. The gate checks each path (plain characters, clean and relative, not under `.ard/`, `.github/` or `.git`), reads main once per tick at one SHA through `ls-tree` (no content, regular blobs only, size capped, cached per SHA) and holds with a \"waiting for inputs\" comment listing each missing path and the capture-note format until every human-provided input exists. A `worker` input with a `network: false` worker role, a bad path or an oversized file ends `needs-human`. A network round always requires a fresh approval, even with `require_approval: false` and even when the engineer removed every network need: the \"ready for approval\" marker gains a `round=<n>`, and an earlier approval is stale because the engineer's new `:done` follows it. An approval given while inputs are missing still counts once they land.\n\"\"\",1)\nopen('docs/proposal.md','w').write(d)\nEOF\ngit diff --stat docs | tail -2; go test ./internal/docscheck/... ./internal/servecmd 2>&1 | tail -5; timeout 300 go test ./internal/roles -run 'Prompt|Network' 2>&1 | tail -3","timeout":400000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_