ck and roles pass; `gofmt` clean. `go vet ./...` only reports an existing testdata file that does not parse. Added tests for the re-arm and lead re-run labels, the round-open and `LeadRerun` logic (including an unclosed worker record), Clear ordering with a 404, the `inputs:` parser, path checks, `decideInputs` (symlink, submodule, size, worker without network), and the gate holding, posting once, then asking for approval with `require_approval: false`. I changed the old rounds test, which asserted that an unclosed record does not count.\n\n## Open issues\n- Not done: the status issue's \"waiting for inputs\" line (the renderer was not located) and the intake test for a re-armed lead being re-claimed. No separate Resume or servecmd test was added.\n- The main fetch for inputs is once per tick, but `planExists` still fetches per issue.\n- The live prompt under `.ard/triage/` is protected; a human must update it to match the starter copy.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_012TMZhEqSmKGm7P2ZueBNAc","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChPpaHoLMhWfm2LgQaJBV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The bounce is now switched on. An engineer `done` in a network round re-arms the lead, the lead re-opens the other triage roles, the gate holds for declared inputs, and a network round always needs a fresh approval. Part of the issue is not done, listed below.\n\nTests pass for `closeout`, `triage`, `gitx`, `servecmd`, `docscheck` and `roles`, and `gofmt` is clean. `go vet ./...` fails on a test-data file that doesn't parse, `internal/roles/testdata/docs/skips/src/_x.go`; I didn't touch it. I didn't run `make lint test`.\n\n- **Round detection:** a round now counts as soon as the worker's close-out is prepared, not only once it is closed, so a crash can no longer skip the fresh approval. I changed the existing rounds test, which asserted the old behaviour.\n- **Lead re-run:** the engineer's close-out clears the lead's `:done` and adds `ard:pending`, and the lead's close-out re-requests the other triage roles that had finished.\n- **Inputs gate:** the engineer's `inputs:` list is read from the redacted role file. The gate reads `main` at one SHA per tick, and holds with a comment listing each missing path.\n- **Approval:** with a network round, \"ready for approval\" is posted even when `require_approval` is false, and the marker carries a `round=<n>` suffix.\n\nNot done:\n- The status issue's \"waiting for inputs\" line. I didn't find the renderer.\n- The intake test that a re-armed lead is re-claimed.\n- A separate Resume test and a `servecmd` test.\n\nThe plan step to move the plan-file check to one fetch per tick is also not done, so `planExists` still fetches once per issue.\n\nThe live engineer prompt under `.ard/triage/` is protected, so a human has to update it to match the starter copy I edited.\n\nThe report is in `.ard/386/worker-engineer.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1199,"cache_read_input_tokens":98748,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1199},"output_tokens":641,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cfd5bca0-cbfd-45b8-a1b8-a24ccd8efc3e","uuid":"c4d2b70b-e4bd-4458-9750-ed6bf1b743ba","timestamp":"2026-11-25T14:41:21.635Z","request_id":"req_011ChPpaHcvMWbCQz6LJ17Yy"}
